title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Start a new workflow
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: A payer with no workflow shows three clear ways to start. A payer that has some reaches the same three through the 'New' button. Every new workflow is a draft; nothing is used for a real case until a person publishes it.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Open Workflow Builder for a payer"
decision d1 "Does the payer have any workflow?"
screen em "Empty state\n'Maple Health Plan has no workflow yet'\nThree cards: 'Start with a template', 'Build from scratch', 'Generate with FLO'\nNote under each: 'Illustrative, not payer policy', 'Full control, more clicks', 'Demo draft: not a live model'"
screen bar "The bar\n'New' menu: 'From a template', 'Blank', 'Generate with FLO'"
click c1 "Click 'Start with a template'\nor New, then 'From a template'"
click c2 "Click 'Build from scratch'\nor New, then 'Blank'"
click c3 "Click 'Generate with FLO'\nor New, then 'Generate with FLO'"
decision d2 "Unsaved changes on the open workflow?"
overlay o0 "'Leave without saving?'"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Workflow Builder › Start from a template"
goto g2 "Continues in: Payers › Workflow Builder › Build from scratch"
goto g3 "Continues in: Payers › Workflow Builder › Generate with FLO"
end e1 "A draft opens on the canvas"

s1 --> d1
d1 -->|No| em
d1 -->|Yes| bar
em --> c1 --> g1
em --> c2 --> g2
em --> c3 --> g3
bar --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| o0 --> c1
d2 -->|No| c1
bar -.-> c2
bar -.-> c3
g1 --> e1
g2 --> e1
g3 --> e1
